<drawables>
    <bitmap id="LauncherIcon" filename="launcher_icon.png"/>
    <bitmap id="RedMoon" filename="moon.png"/>

    <!-- Star sprites for the bright tiers. Grayscale on opaque black: the
         field draws straight onto Theme.BG (always 0x000000) right after
         dc.clear, so nothing behind them needs preserving and no transparency
         is required. drawBitmap2's :tintColor scales by luminance, so white
         comes out at the star's full colour and the sparkle's 45% grey
         diagonals come out at 45% of it - one call for the whole sprite.

         automaticPalette="false" is required: drawBitmap2 refuses a
         palettised source ("Source must not use a color palette"), the same
         restriction the rotated second-numeral labels hit in renderLabel.

         Sizes are fixed pixels, not scaled(): Dial.scaled(2) and scaled(3)
         both round to the same value on venu3 (r=227) and venu3s (r=195), so
         one sprite per tier serves both watches.

         Tier 0's 3x3 is the same two-stroke cross the code used to draw by
         hand. It was left out on the strength of a benchmark that turned out
         to have been run with anti-aliasing off; on a Venu 3 a blit and a
         stroke cost the same, so one call beats two. See docs/track-perf.md. -->
    <bitmap id="Star3" filename="star_3x3.png" automaticPalette="false"/>
    <bitmap id="Star5" filename="star_5x5.png" automaticPalette="false"/>
    <bitmap id="Star7" filename="star_7x7.png" automaticPalette="false"/>
</drawables>
